# ============================================================================
# Chronicle .gitignore
# ============================================================================
# This file controls what Git ignores. Organized by category.
# Category: Static -- rarely needs changes.
# ============================================================================

# --- Go ---
# Compiled binary
/chronicle
/server
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool
*.out
*.prof
coverage.html

# Go workspace file
go.work.local

# --- Templ (generated Go files from .templ sources) ---
*_templ.go

# --- sqlc (generated Go files from SQL queries) ---
# NOTE: If we ever adopt sqlc, uncomment this:
# db/sqlc/

# --- Tailwind CSS (generated output) ---
static/css/app.css

# --- Environment & Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- IDE / Editor ---
.idea/
.vscode/
# Claude Code scratch worktrees — throwaway checkouts, never repo state.
# Only the worktrees dir: .claude/ itself holds TRACKED project config
# (.claude/hooks/session-start.sh), so ignoring the parent would silently
# hide a real, versioned file.
.claude/worktrees/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
Thumbs.db

# --- Docker ---
# Don't ignore docker-compose.yml or Dockerfile (those are tracked)

# --- Node (Tailwind CLI & plugins) ---
node_modules/

# --- Temporary / Build ---
tmp/
dist/
/bin/

# --- OS / System files ---
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# --- Log files ---
*.log

# --- Uploads (user-generated content in dev) ---
uploads/

# --- Runtime data directory (C-SWEEP, 2026-08-16) ---
#
# The server creates ./data at boot when run from the repo root: MediaRoot
# defaults there and the media-signing SECRET is written to data/.signing-secret.
# Neither is source. Untracked-but-not-ignored is the dangerous middle state —
# it survives every `git status` review as noise and then rides along on the
# first `git add -A`, which is how a signing key reaches a public remote.
#
# Verified at the time of writing: nothing under data/ had ever been committed
# on any branch (`git log --all -- data/` was empty). This keeps it that way.
data/
